    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4162\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the county of Tompkins\nto continue imposing an additional one percent sales tax\n\nPURPOSE:\nTo extend for two more years statutory authorization to Tompkins\nCounty to impose an additional one percent sales and compensating use\ntax.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nAmends Section 1210 of the tax law.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nTompkins County has formally requested this authorization to impose\nthe additional sales tax be extended for two years. The extension is\nnecessary in order to avoid a $10,050,000 reduction in county\nexpenditures which would create a major impact on the availability of\nservices or would impose a 25% increase in County property taxes.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
